{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-tsx","path":"/blog/2023-01-16--ieee-transactions-on-software-engineering-2021-best-paper-award/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"disqus":"edward-j-schwartz"}},"post":{"html":"<p>Right before the holidays, I, along with my co-authors of the journal article <em>The Art, Science, and Engineering of Fuzzing: A Survey</em>, received an early holiday present!</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Congratulations!</p>\n<p>On behalf of Vice President for Publications, David Ebert, I am writing to inform you that your paper, \"The Art, Science, and Engineering of Fuzzing: A Survey,\" has been awarded the 2021 Best Paper Award from IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering by the IEEE Computer Society Publications Board.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This was quite unexpected, as our article was accepted back in 2019 -- four years ago!  But it only \"appeared\" in the November 2021 editions of the journal.</p>\n<p>You can access this article <a href=\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/8863940\">here</a> or, as always, on my <a href=\"/publications\">publications page</a>.</p>","excerpt":"Right before the holidays, I, along with my co-authors of the journal article The Art, Science, and Engineering of Fuzzing: A Survey…","timeToRead":1,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2023-01-16--ieee-transactions-on-software-engineering-2021-best-paper-award/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["papers","publications","fuzzing"],"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","twitter":"@edmcman","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png 80w","sizes":"80px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/1deab/ed.webp 80w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"80px"}]},"width":80,"height":80}}}},"title":"\"Th